# Design system (Cartesia)

Canonical spec: **`docs/DESIGN.md`** (moved out of `.tmp/`; do not put it back in scratch).

## When this fires

Any UI, layout, theme tokens, typography, color, spacing, or component chrome work under `src/`.

## How to apply

1. Read `docs/DESIGN.md` for tokens (`colors`, type, spacing, motion) before inventing styles.
2. Prefer CSS variables / a single theme module mapped from DESIGN tokens — do not hardcode one-off hex that contradicts the spec.
3. **Canvas / page background:** use DESIGN `bg` / `bg-soft` (Cartesia clinical white), **not** Labs root `#f3f3f3`, unless the user asks otherwise.
4. Brand / actions: DESIGN `brand` (`#2563eb`) and CTA rules from the spec; keep the “one deep blue + near-monochrome” language.
5. UI copy stays **Russian for the end user** — see `.cursor/rules/ui-copy.mdc`. **Ignore DESIGN §11 English marketing voice** for app strings.
6. Prefer existing `src/lib/components/ui/*` (Button variants: `primary|secondary|danger|ghost`) over one-off controls. DESIGN `button-blue` maps to app `primary`.
7. App density ≠ marketing hero scale in DESIGN; do not paste 96px display rhythm into `/app/*`.
8. If DESIGN and a product decision conflict, ask — do not silently diverge.
9. **Tailwind v4 class canon** (avoids `suggestCanonicalClasses` noise):
   - Important modifier: **postfix only** — `px-3!`, `hover:bg-surface!`. Never prefix `!px-3` / `hover:!bg-surface` (deprecated).
   - Prefer scale utilities over equivalent arbitrary values when IntelliSense offers them — e.g. `rounded-md` not `rounded-[6px]`, `min-w-48` not `min-w-[12rem]`, `pb-13` not `pb-[3.25rem]`. Keep arbitrary values only when no named scale token fits (design tokens like `rounded-[8px]` matching `--radius-control` are OK until themed utilities exist).

## Do not

- Treat `.tmp/` as the home for DESIGN.md.
- Load the full DESIGN.md on non-UI tasks (this rule is glob-scoped on purpose).
- Add a second competing design system without user approval.
- Write Tailwind v3-style prefix important (`!utility`) in new or edited UI.
